## Summary

I have created a comprehensive research proposal for **Project A.I.D. (Algorithmic Integrity and Distribution)** and saved it to `/app/research/report.md`. The document contains all required sections:

| Section | Location | Description |
|---------|----------|-------------|
| **Title** | Line 16 | Full project title with subtitle describing the novel behavioral-signature framework |
| **Assumptions** | Line 6 | 5 bullet points covering dataset characteristics, ground truth availability, stakeholder access, computational resources, and team composition |
| **Background & Motivation** | Line 24 | Three subsections covering the challenge, innovation gap, and policy mandate (7 CFR Part 272, NIST AI RMF) |
| **Objectives** | Line 60 | Primary objective (BSRS Model) and 5 secondary objectives with specific performance targets |
| **Methodology / Technical Approach** | Line 83 | Four-phase research design with the core innovation: three novel behavioral economics constructs (Temporal Budget Adherence, Retailer Diversity & Specialization, Temporal Stability and Habitual Pattern Disruption), logistic regression and decision tree models with XAI integration |
| **Risks, Ethics, and Safety Considerations** | Line 202 | Five subsections covering data privacy, algorithmic fairness, misclassification risk, ethical use of behavioral economics, and scalability risks |
| **Deliverables & Timeline** | Line 235 | Four milestones over 12 months with detailed deliverable descriptions and Gantt-chart visualization |
| **References** | Line 287 | 12 references including recent fraud detection literature, NIST AI RMF, and USDA policy documents |

### Key Innovations in the Proposal

1. **Truly Novel Methodology**: Introduces the **Behavioral-Signature Risk Scoring (BSRS)** framework—no prior work has applied behavioral economics concepts (mental accounting, consumer choice theory, habit formation) to EBT transaction analysis.

2. **9 New Behavioral Indicators**: Three constructs × 3 features each, including Budget Velocity Index, Temporal Gini Coefficient, Retailer Concentration Index, and Pattern Stability Score.

3. **Explainable-by-Design**: Uses logistic regression with Elastic Net and decision trees—both inherently interpretable—as required by NIST AI RMF.

4. **Audit-Ready**: Risk Score Explanation Reports (RSER) provide feature-level attribution for every flagged account.
